cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its evidence, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Financial ABM: an auditable multi-agent artificial market for ESG disclosure and greenwashing policy experiments"
abstract: >-
  An agent-based artificial financial market in which profit-maximizing and impact investors
  evolve by imitation, firms choose between real improvement, greenwashing and maintenance,
  and a regulator sets transparency, audits and fines. The disclosure domain (ESG, AI-washing, ...)
  is a configuration file. It contains the pre-registered stage F experiment (59 scenarios x 30
  paired seeds), in which information policy ranks above penalty policy and baseline at the tested
  doses, its exploratory supplements, and a static browser sandbox whose firm decision rule is
  cross-checked against the Python model. Version 0.3.0 adds pre-registered experiments on targeted
  audits, assurance providers and learning firms, and a pre-registered joint robustness test: the
  ordering holds in all four joint settings, but with mean reversion of true levels and a fine for
  every false report, information beats penalty by only 0.004 to 0.012 SD. It also adds the working
  paper and a check of what the public repository alone can rebuild. Results are conditional on the
  model.
